Basic goal:
	Something akin to a fancy new OS from 1985/1986 for the IBM PC/AT or Amstrad PC1512
	Assume only around 512kb RAM (up to  0x80000)
	

Tasks:
	per-task arenas of 64kb (CS=DS=ES=SS)

Kernel:
	Lives at segment 1000h - that would be physical 0x10000

Tasks live at 2000h up to 7000h
Each task occupies 1000h (e.g one 64kb segment)

Two floppies:
	Kernel+Bootloader floppy
		Not FAT - very simple dump of kernel image to raw sectors
		Simple little MBR
